        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/da81d3f6-198e-4f2f-935c-d0ee58ed0a3c,1784224177623/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C265%2C1803%2C1014%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='Horses stand in snow.' width='620' height='349' title='Przewalski&apos;s horses near the Red Forest in the Chornobyl exclusion zone in 2021. Considered the last truly wild species of horse, the endangered animals have been affected by remilitarization in the once-vacated area, and have been killed by anti-tank mines.'/><p>From Chornobyl's endangered wild horses to bird nests made of drone cables, modern warfare is reshaping fragile ecosystems along Ukraine\u2019s front lines.</p>",
